  "title": "Kourovka problem 17.4 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let x be a right 4-Engel element of a group G.\n    a) Is it true that the normal closure ⟨x⟩G of x in G is nilpotent if G is locally\nnilpotent?\n    b) If the answer to a) is affirmative, is there a bound on the nilpotency class\nof ⟨x⟩G ?\n    c) Is it true that ⟨x⟩G is always nilpotent?                        A. Abdollahi",
